      "tool": "Mechanism",
      "text": "Fischer esterification mechanism\n\nAcid-catalysed ester formation from acetic acid and ethanol in six states: protonation, addition, proton transfer and loss of water, all reversible.\n\nFischer esterification: 2 reactant(s) → 2 product(s), 6 states.\nStates: Reactants → Protonated acid → Addition → Proton transfer → Loss of water → Products.\nOverall ΔH = -3 kJ/mol; highest transition state 40 kJ/mol above the reactants (the rate-determining step is Protonated acid → Addition).\nOpens at the addition step (state 3 of 6): the alcohol has attacked the protonated carbonyl; step back and forward to follow the proton shuffling.",
